# 5.restore-parallelism

diagnose why the suite runs serial, fix the CAUSE, raise the worker count.

.guard = the full suite runs green at the raised worker count, and compare reports
  zero lost cases. a red run here is a cause to find, never a retry to spend.

.hardwon = CHECK THE PROVENANCE of a constraint — and then TEST it anyway. the config
  carried `maxWorkers: 1` with the note "symlink race conditions in temp dir setup".
  `git log -S maxWorkers` put it in the repos FIRST import commit: inherited lore,
  never diagnosed here. I concluded it was a rut and raised it to 8.
  595 cases failed. the constraint was REAL. provenance told me the note was
  undiagnosed; it did not tell me the note was wrong.

.hardwon = the note named the wrong mechanism, which is why it read as lore. the true
  cause is resource exhaustion, not a logic race: fs.existsSync returns FALSE on any
  error, EMFILE included. under 8 workers on 4 cores, each case spawning bash -> rhx ->
  bun, the existsSync(dist) check inside test-fns createSymlinks fails spuriously and
  reports "symlink target not found: <gitroot>/dist". dist was there the whole time.

.hardwon = a failure that only appears at FULL SCALE will not reproduce in a scoped
  run. 4 files at 8 workers: 263/263 green. 117 files at 8 workers: 595 red. scope down
  to debug, but never conclude from a scoped green.

.hardwon = worker count is set by how many WAITS can be in flight, bounded by fds and
  memory — not by core count alone.
